  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "New eQTL catalogs, imputation panels and sequence-model scores expand diverse-population coverage and improve noncoding variant prioritization.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is prioritizing regulatory variants through better models and denser population resources. Methods include eQIF, which uses unsupervised isolation forests over Enformer predictions; Borzoi fine-tuned on synthetic MPRA labels, which raises CAGI5 and eQTL correlations; and XGBoost-SHAP on snATAC-seq to flag HNF4A motif-disrupting SNPs. mV2G integrates 24 evidence types across 50 tissues with a CRISPR-informed model. Resource and statistical advances complement these: a Qatar Biobank transcriptome QTL catalog with 1,379 novel eGenes, SAIGE-QTL for single-cell eQTL mapping, and a 490,319-genome UK Biobank reference panel that improves imputation. A heritability analysis in 198,931 diverse individuals reports substantial rare and non-coding contributions. The items are heterogeneous, but all aim to resolve variant effects across ancestries and tissues.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
